{
  "id": "server.jobs.list",
  "method": "GET",
  "path": "/api/jobs",
  "summary": "Every job the bound folder holds, in the order they were submitted; `queue_pos` gives each queued job its place in line. A batch job planned for later carries its `not_before`, and one waiting for room on the card says so in its `progress` (S18): both are `queued`, and neither holds back the jobs behind them. Jobs on different models answer at the same time, each model one at a time: every one of them is `running`, with its own `progress`. `?scope=<key>` narrows the list to the jobs submitted with that scope. `?client=<actor id>` narrows it to the jobs one client asked for. Each is given once or not at all, and a client is an actor id: a client that is not one, or one given twice, is refused `bad_client`, and a scope given twice `bad_scope` - a list narrowed by one of two values would be a guess. Either is refused before anything is asked of the queue: a question that is malformed is malformed whether or not a folder is bound, and a query is not a body, so it is never `bad_request`. A value left blank (`?client=`) counts as not given.",
  "request": null,
  "responses": {
    "200": {"object": {"jobs": {"array": {"ref": "job"}}}},
    "400": {"object": {"error": "string", "reason": {"enum": ["bad_client", "bad_scope"]}}},
    "409": {"object": {"error": "string", "reason": {"enum": ["no_workspace"]}}},
    "503": {"object": {"error": "string", "reason": {"enum": ["store_unreadable"]}}}
  },
